# Lucy RP2040 controller board — serial access without group membership.
#
# Installed to /etc/udev/rules.d/ by install.py. The firmware declares this
# VID/PID in firmwares/rp2040/src/main.rs (UsbVidPid(0x16c0, 0x27dd)), and the
# host-side bridge scans for the same pair.
#
# Without this rule the board lands as root:dialout 0660, so opening it needs
# dialout membership — which a login session picks up only after a full
# re-login, and which a long-lived tmux server never picks up at all. The
# embedded bridge then dies on "Permission denied" opening /dev/ttyACM0.
#
# MODE="0666" is deliberate: it works over SSH and in headless or containerised
# sessions, where TAG+="uaccess" grants nothing because there is no active local
# seat. The trade-off is that any local user can open the board's serial port.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="16c0", ATTRS{idProduct}=="27dd", MODE="0666", TAG+="uaccess"
